<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Instead of considering the size of <math id="S4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> directly where every word is uniformly weighted, we use these coefficients <math id="S4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> to assign different weights to the words in <math id="S4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, resulting in a better-behaved total weight of <math id="S4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Denote</p>
