<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha\widehat{C_{n}}-\sum_{i=p+1}^{n+1}\widehat{C_{n+1-i}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha\widehat{C_{n}}-\sum_{i=p+1}^{n+1}\widehat{C_{n+1-i}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We now prove the main ingredient in the proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ There exist infinite cube-free words over any sequence of binary alphabets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 13</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha-\frac{\beta^{1-p}}{\beta-1}\geq\beta," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha-\frac{\beta^{1-p}}{\beta-1}\geq\beta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem13.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem13.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">then for every <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{C_{n}}\geq\beta\widehat{C_{n-1}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{C_{n}}\geq\beta\widehat{C_{n-1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove it for every <math id="S4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> using strong induction method.
Assume the hypothesis holds up to some <math id="S4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, that is, <math id="S4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{C_{i}}\geq\beta\widehat{C_{i-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{C_{i}}\geq\beta\widehat{C_{i-1}}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="S4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>. We need to show that <math id="S4.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{C_{n+1}}\geq\beta\widehat{C_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{C_{n+1}}\geq\beta\widehat{C_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the induction hypothesis, we have <math id="S4.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{C_{n+1-i}}\leq\beta^{1-i}\widehat{C_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{C_{n+1-i}}\leq\beta^{1-i}\widehat{C_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>, for all <math id="S4.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. It follows from Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem12" title="Lemma 12. ‣ 4 Cube-free words grow exponentially ‣ There exist infinite cube-free words over any sequence of binary alphabets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> that</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{C_{n+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{C_{n+1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\alpha\widehat{C_{n}}-\sum_{i=p+1}^{n+1}\widehat{C_{n+1-i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\alpha\widehat{C_{n}}-\sum_{i=p+1}^{n+1}\widehat{C_{n+1-i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\alpha\widehat{C_{n}}-\sum_{i=p+1}^{n+1}\beta^{1-i}\widehat{C_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\alpha\widehat{C_{n}}-\sum_{i=p+1}^{n+1}\beta^{1-i}\widehat{C_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\alpha\widehat{C_{n}}-\sum_{i\geq p+1}\beta^{1-i}\widehat{C_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\alpha\widehat{C_{n}}-\sum_{i\geq p+1}\beta^{1-i}\widehat{C_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\alpha-\frac{\beta^{1-p}}{\beta-1}\right)\widehat{C_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\alpha-\frac{\beta^{1-p}}{\beta-1}\right)\widehat{C_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\beta\widehat{C_{n}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\beta\widehat{C_{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">We finish the induction step and conclude that <math id="S4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{C_{n}}\geq\beta\widehat{C_{n-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{C_{n}}\geq\beta\widehat{C_{n-1}}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="S4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1.457" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.457</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1.457</annotation></semantics></math>, we set</p>
<table id="S4.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1.35" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.35</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1.35</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p8.2" class="ltx_p">to satisfy the condition <math id="S4.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha-\frac{\beta^{1-p}}{\beta-1}\geq\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha-\frac{\beta^{1-p}}{\beta-1}\geq\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.
It follows by induction that</p>
<table id="S4.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{C_{n}}\geq\beta^{n}\widehat{C_{0}}=\lambda_{\epsilon}\beta^{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{C_{n}}\geq\beta^{n}\widehat{C_{0}}=\lambda_{\epsilon}\beta^{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p8.3" class="ltx_p">Now we are ready to prove Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ There exist infinite cube-free words over any sequence of binary alphabets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ There exist infinite cube-free words over any sequence of binary alphabets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="S4.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Denoting <math id="S4.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{*}=\max_{s}\lambda_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{*}=\max_{s}\lambda_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|C_{n}|=\sum_{s}|C_{n}^{s}|=\frac{1}{\lambda^{*}}\sum_{s}\lambda^{*}|C_{n}^{s}|\geq\frac{1}{\lambda^{*}}\sum_{s}\lambda_{s}|C_{n}^{s}|=\frac{1}{\lambda^{*}}\widehat{C_{n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>s</mi></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>s</mi></munder><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>s</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|C_{n}|=\sum_{s}|C_{n}^{s}|=\frac{1}{\lambda^{*}}\sum_{s}\lambda^{*}|C_{n}^{s}|\geq\frac{1}{\lambda^{*}}\sum_{s}\lambda_{s}|C_{n}^{s}|=\frac{1}{\lambda^{*}}\widehat{C_{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">It follows that</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|C_{n}|\geq\frac{1}{\lambda^{*}}\widehat{C_{n}}\geq\frac{\lambda_{\epsilon}}{\lambda^{*}}\beta^{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|C_{n}|\geq\frac{1}{\lambda^{*}}\widehat{C_{n}}\geq\frac{\lambda_{\epsilon}}{\lambda^{*}}\beta^{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">In other words, the number of cube-free words in <math id="S4.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is at least a constant times <math id="S4.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. It follows that <math id="S4.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is a lower bound on the growth rate <math id="S4.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.
On the other hand, we know that <math id="S4.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|C_{n}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|C_{n}|</annotation></semantics></math> is submultiplicative, in the sense that <math id="S4.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|C_{\ell+m}|\leq|C_{\ell}||C_{m}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|C_{\ell+m}|\leq|C_{\ell}||C_{m}|</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="S4.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell,m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell,m</annotation></semantics></math>. By Fekete’s lemma, <math id="S4.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|C_{n}|\geq\alpha^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|C_{n}|\geq\alpha^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="S4.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>. In total,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|C_{n}|\geq\alpha^{n}\geq\beta^{n}=1.35^{n}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>1.35</mn><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|C_{n}|\geq\alpha^{n}\geq\beta^{n}=1.35^{n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">which concludes Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ There exist infinite cube-free words over any sequence of binary alphabets" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
